wifi: brcmfmac: send other action frames without the retry delay (local)

brcmf_p2p_send_action_frame() sleeps P2P_AF_RETRY_DELAY_TIME (40 ms)
before every attempt when a channel is set, including the first. That
delay belongs to the P2P/GAS exchanges; for the other action frames
patch 0004 now sends (Splanc's vendor-specific Public Action mesh
frames), it makes each NL80211_CMD_FRAME block ~50 ms instead of the
~5-10 ms the firmware round trip takes.

Skip the delay before the first attempt for those frames only. P2P
public action, GAS and P2P action frames keep it, and a retry of any
frame still waits.

Local to Splanc's Pi images (pi/provisioning/nix/brcmfmac-actframe.nix),
not part of the upstream series. Applies on top of 0001-0005.

Tested on a Pi 3B+ (CYW43455, fw 7.45.265, 6.12.87), A/B against
0001-0005 with 100 frames each: unicast send p50 54.8 -> 8.8 ms (all
ACKed), broadcast 51.2 -> 5.7 ms, ping/pong RTT p50 61.8 -> 18.0 ms;
an absent peer still gets 20/20 NO_ACK after its retries.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
@@ -1743,6 +1743,7 @@
 	uint delta_ms;
 	unsigned long dwell_jiffies = 0;
 	bool dwell_overflow = false;
+	bool p2p_af = true;
 
 	u32 requested_dwell = le32_to_cpu(af_params->dwell_time);
 	action_frame = &af_params->action_frame;
@@ -1812,6 +1813,7 @@
 			  category, action);
 		af_params->dwell_time =
 			cpu_to_le32(requested_dwell & ~CUSTOM_RETRY_MASK);
+		p2p_af = false;
 	}
 
 	/* if connecting on primary iface, sleep for a while before sending
@@ -1871,7 +1873,10 @@
 	while (!p2p->block_gon_req_tx &&
 	       (!ack) && (tx_retry < P2P_AF_TX_MAX_RETRY) &&
 		!dwell_overflow) {
-		if (af_params->channel)
+		/* P2P and GAS exchanges wait before every attempt. Other
+		 * action frames go out at once; their retries still wait.
+		 */
+		if (af_params->channel && (p2p_af || tx_retry))
 			msleep(P2P_AF_RETRY_DELAY_TIME);
 
 		ack = !brcmf_p2p_tx_action_frame(ifp, p2p, af_params);
